# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ARPBOX — Git attributes
#
# Scope note: this file intentionally does NOT set a repo-wide `* text=auto`.
# That has checkout-wide implications for every tracked file and belongs in its
# own deliberate change, not smuggled in alongside the golden format.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Determinism goldens (ARCHITECTURE §1.2, docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md Phase 6.4) ────
# tests/golden/ holds the reference MIDI event streams the determinism gate
# compares against, in the canonical text format documented in
# tests/golden/README.md. Force LF on checkout AND on checkin:
#
#   • The comparison is byte-exact on the parsed event stream, and the loader in
#     tests/support/GoldenMidiFile.h REJECTS a carriage return outright. A CRLF
#     checkout would turn every golden into a parse error.
#   • This is not theoretical: a Windows port is on the §2.2 roadmap, and
#     core.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default.
#
# Deliberately NOT set here:
#   • `linguist-generated` — it collapses the diff on GitHub, which is the exact
#     opposite of what "a golden diff is a FINDING" needs. The diff must be read.
#   • a merge driver — a conflict in a golden should be LOUD and resolved by a
#     human deciding which performance is correct, never auto-merged.
tests/golden/** text eol=lf
